From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 10:36:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: check SKU control results, use per-chip WDUCR

The radio start sends the SKU limit control and then the backoff
limit control, but checks only the result of the second command.
Upstream 5a9b590919a6 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: enable the SKU power
limit table") returns the error of the first command, and the port
of the debug tools lost that check. Return each error.

The WTBL debugfs readers write the LMAC group to a fixed WDUCR
address. Since a8def214d736 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: rework register
mapping for mt7990"), MT7990 has WDUCR at another offset, so on that
chip the readers write the group to another register and dump the
wrong entry for a WLAN index of 128 or more. Use the per-chip
register.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/main.c        |    5 +++++
 mt7996/mtk_debugfs.c |    8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -55,12 +55,17 @@ int mt7996_run(struct mt7996_phy *phy)
 
 	ret = mt7996_mcu_set_tx_power_ctrl(phy, UNI_TXPOWER_SKU_POWER_LIMIT_CTRL,
 						dev->dbg.sku_disable ? 0 : phy->sku_limit_en);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	ret = mt7996_mcu_set_tx_power_ctrl(phy, UNI_TXPOWER_BACKOFF_POWER_LIMIT_CTRL,
 						dev->dbg.sku_disable ? 0 : phy->sku_path_en);
 #else
 	ret = mt7996_mcu_set_tx_power_ctrl(phy, UNI_TXPOWER_SKU_POWER_LIMIT_CTRL,
 						phy->sku_limit_en);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	ret = mt7996_mcu_set_tx_power_ctrl(phy, UNI_TXPOWER_BACKOFF_POWER_LIMIT_CTRL,
 						phy->sku_path_en);
 #endif
--- a/mt7996/mtk_debugfs.c
+++ b/mt7996/mtk_debugfs.c
@@ -875,8 +875,8 @@ mt7996_wtbl_read_raw(struct mt7996_dev *
 		return 0xFF;
 
 	if (type == WTBL_TYPE_LMAC) {
-		mt76_wr(dev, MT_DBG_WTBLON_TOP_WDUCR_ADDR,
-			FIELD_PREP(MT_DBG_WTBLON_TOP_WDUCR_GROUP, (idx >> 7)));
+		mt76_wr(dev, MT_WTBLON_TOP_WDUCR,
+			FIELD_PREP(MT_WTBLON_TOP_WDUCR_GROUP, (idx >> 7)));
 		src = LWTBL_IDX2BASE(idx, start_dw);
 	} else if (type == WTBL_TYPE_UMAC) {
 		mt76_wr(dev,  MT_DBG_UWTBL_TOP_WDUCR_ADDR,
@@ -2256,8 +2256,8 @@ static int mt7996_wtbl_read(struct seq_f
 				 LWTBL_LEN_IN_DW, lwtbl);
 	seq_printf(s, "Dump WTBL info of WLAN_IDX:%d\n", dev->wlan_idx);
 	seq_printf(s, "LMAC WTBL Addr: group:0x%x=0x%x addr: 0x%lx\n",
-		   MT_DBG_WTBLON_TOP_WDUCR_ADDR,
-		   mt76_rr(dev, MT_DBG_WTBLON_TOP_WDUCR_ADDR),
+		   MT_WTBLON_TOP_WDUCR,
+		   mt76_rr(dev, MT_WTBLON_TOP_WDUCR),
 		   LWTBL_IDX2BASE(dev->wlan_idx, 0));
 	for (x = 0; x < LWTBL_LEN_IN_DW; x++) {
 		seq_printf(s, "DW%02d: %02x %02x %02x %02x\n",
